Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Nate-Bargatze.md` (~4,071 body words) against the entity-gap packet and the research doc. Fresh-eyes notes appended at the bottom of the file. No body edits.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **The flunked-out section builds a Nine read on facts he has publicly explained differently.** Bargatze has said on the record he was diagnosed with ADHD as an adult. The research doc flags it with a "do not build a typology claim on it" warning, and the draft handled that by leaving it out entirely — so the section argues a psychological stall using "He just didn't show up" with no competing account in the room. Omitting it is weaker than naming it and attributing it to him. This is the draft's most one-sided passage and it comes early enough to cost reader trust for everything after.

2. **His mother is not in the piece at all.** Carol Bargatze has a full first-person podcast episode on the record, and her best line is already sitting unused in the research doc — she calls the family the "Christianiest Christians." The childhood section is a closed loop between father and son, yet the clean-act origin turns on both parents being in the room. Her line would also fix the draft's other soft spot: the faith frame is asserted ("second to God") but never established, so a reader can't tell whether the self-effacement is religious or temperamental.

Also flagged: the hand/misdirection metaphor fires five times and the park section's "Watch the hand move" pre-empts the closer; the Breadwinner section resolves a tension the packet asked to leave open and never lets him speak about the reviews; three contrast-pair fragments cluster in the final section despite the ledger's "0 strong" (the scripts don't catch that shape); and the MBTI half of the database argument the packet requires is missing. Four facts are marked verify-before-next-pass, including the $20M/$25M film financials the packet lists as unverified.
